--- Maps a function over a list and flattens the results one level.
---
--- @details
--- `flat_map` takes `[f, xs]` and returns the concatenation of `f(x)`
--- for each `x` in `xs`. When `f(x)` is a list its elements are spliced
--- into the output; any other value is appended as-is. It is the
--- collection counterpart of `comb.pipe`'s per-element application and
--- the `comb`-surface spelling of `combinators.flat_map`.
---
--- @example
--- `[x ~> [x, x * 2], [1, 2, 3]] >>> comb.flat_map`
--- -- => [1, 2, 2, 4, 3, 6]
---
export flat_map := [f, xs] ~> combinators.flat_map(f, xs)
